# S5720S-28TP-PWR-LI-ACL / V200R019C10SPC500, 2026-10-14
# SOURCE-ONLY candidate. The destination-exemption candidate was rejected by hardware.
# Confirmed: VLAN1 single-client IPv6 source PBR to nanopi5 WAN works.
# Confirmed: VLAN2 single-client source PBR to nanopc WAN works.
# Confirmed: VLAN2->A ping and SSH banner passed with scoped temporary B firewall rules.
# Those temporary rules were removed; the persistent /64 firewall fragments are candidates.
# Confirmed: reverse VLAN1->B ping and SSH banner passed with scoped temporary A rules.
# Both temporary rule sets were removed; broader internal services and /64 remain untested.
# The /64 deployment template is huawei-s5720s-ipv6-pbr-production.cli.example.
# Internal packets matching these rules also go to the selected edge router.
# The edge must route them BACK TO THE CORE via br-lan, without NAT/proxy interception.
# Keep Vlanif3/4 outside this PBR, so returned packets do not loop to the edge again.
# Current edge firewall permits LAN hairpin to its own PD pool, not the opposite pool.
# Cross-group internal forwarding therefore requires separately scoped firewall rules.
# Do not expand to /64 or save until routes, firewall and real-client tests pass.
# Existing security ACLs continue to govern authorized internal access.
# Fixed prefixes below are PD snapshots; update them after an actual prefix change.
# Initial /128 rules test only the selected clients; /64 expansion is commented below.
# VLAN1 Mac test without RA initially lacked an en0 on-link route.
# Even after adding that route, global-core next-hop tests still failed locally.
# Using the core link-local gateway fe80::fa98:efff:fe77:6450%en0 succeeded.
# Prefer that link-local gateway for test host routes, as normal RA-based clients do.
# User terminal (sudo required), only if that route is absent:
# sudo route -n add -inet6 -net -ifscope en0 2408:8207:7866:a785::/64 -interface en0
# Clean up only routes added by this test when finished (including the /64 if added).

# STAGE 1: Create UNBOUND source-only objects, reusing ACL3981/3982 from prior candidate.
# Confirm those ACLs contain only the intended rule 5 before replacing it.
system-view
acl ipv6 3981
 undo rule 5
 rule 5 permit ipv6 source 2408:8207:7866:a785::c0de:1014 128
 quit
acl ipv6 3982
 undo rule 5
 rule 5 permit ipv6 source 2408:8207:7865:78b1:14b7:e9c6:ea47:e554 128
 quit
traffic classifier PBR6_A_SOURCE operator or
 if-match ipv6 acl 3981
 quit
traffic classifier PBR6_B_SOURCE operator or
 if-match ipv6 acl 3982
 quit
traffic behavior PBR6_TO_A
 redirect ipv6-nexthop link-local FE80::B83B:17FF:FE74:32D0 interface Vlanif 3
 statistics enable
 quit
traffic behavior PBR6_TO_B
 redirect ipv6-nexthop link-local FE80::5434:4EFF:FEFA:68A4 interface Vlanif 4
 statistics enable
 quit
traffic policy PBR6_A_EGRESS
 classifier PBR6_A_SOURCE behavior PBR6_TO_A
 quit
traffic policy PBR6_B_EGRESS
 classifier PBR6_B_SOURCE behavior PBR6_TO_B
 quit
return

# STAGE 2: Single-client tests. Each stage needs actual hardware success.
# The failed destination-based interface binding must first be removed if present.
# system-view
# interface GigabitEthernet 0/0/4
#  undo traffic-policy PBR6_EGRESS inbound
#  quit
# vlan 1
#  undo traffic-policy PBR6_A_SRC_PROBE inbound
#  traffic-policy PBR6_A_EGRESS inbound
#  quit
# vlan 2
#  undo traffic-policy PBR6_B_SRC_PROBE inbound
#  traffic-policy PBR6_B_EGRESS inbound
#  quit
# return
# display traffic-policy applied-record
# Test both WAN paths and authorized internal TCP/UDP/ICMPv6, not just ping.
# Verify ND/RA and OSPFv3 health; verify internal traffic does not enter either WAN.

# STAGE 3: Only after edge rules and /128 tests pass, expand sources to whole VLANs.
# system-view
# acl ipv6 3981
#  undo rule 5
#  rule 5 permit ipv6 source 2408:8207:7866:a785:: 64
#  quit
# acl ipv6 3982
#  undo rule 5
#  rule 5 permit ipv6 source 2408:8207:7865:78b1:: 64
#  quit
# return
# save  <-- only after final validation

# ROLLBACK: Restore the known test bindings, with their then-current /128 ACLs.
# system-view
# vlan 1
#  undo traffic-policy PBR6_A_EGRESS inbound
#  traffic-policy PBR6_A_SRC_PROBE inbound
#  quit
# vlan 2
#  undo traffic-policy PBR6_B_EGRESS inbound
#  traffic-policy PBR6_B_SRC_PROBE inbound
#  quit
# return
# Remove only the temporary edge rules created for this test, by their recorded handles.
# Enabling VLAN1 RA is separate: verify its current PD/PIO before enabling it.
